                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "What does this mean? Is this not a bug in the driver?\n\nWhat driver is affected?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "This is the power supply driver for IBM System1. But if a user doesn't have the PSU fan sensors in their entity-manager config label (https://grok.openbmc.org/xref/openbmc/entity-manager/configurations/system1_psu.json?r=075ad3f478655adc3e6d32cae10d9440b79641fe#7) then it shouldn't be added to dbus-sensors. Or am I misunderstanding something here?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "> But if a user doesn't have the PSU fan sensors in their entity-manager config label (https://grok.openbmc.org/xref/openbmc/entity-manager/configurations/system1_psu.json?r=075ad3f478655adc3e6d32cae10d9440b79641fe#7) then it shouldn't be added to dbus-sensors.\n\nThat seems reasonable. However, what you've written in the commit message makes it sound like you're working around a bug in the driver. Can you please rephrase it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
